WEBVTT

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:12.751
Inventory keeps stock at each location up to date, and tells you what to order. In this video, you’ll receive a delivery, count the walk-in, act on suggestions, and see which dishes earn the most.

00:00:13.833 --> 00:00:22.815
Open Inventory and pick a location. Every item is listed by category, with what’s low or out first, how many days it will last, and its par.

00:00:23.267 --> 00:00:30.968
Each row has Count, Received and Waste. The oat milk just arrived, so click Received. Enter it the way it came: three cases.

00:00:31.433 --> 00:00:38.559
Worklynq converts it to thirty-six cartons, and shows what’s on hand after. Save, and it’s on record, with who did it.

00:00:39.333 --> 00:00:46.864
The Count tab is made for walking the walk-in. Type what’s on each shelf, press Enter to jump to the next, and save once at the end.

00:00:47.633 --> 00:00:58.215
Suggestions reads what sold, from Square and Order Tracking, and turns it into what to order, pars to change, and counts that don’t add up. Each shows the numbers behind it.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:07.853
That works through menu links. A link says what one sale uses, so an almond croissant uses one croissant. Link a menu item in seconds.

00:01:08.633 --> 00:01:20.047
Profit shows what each dish costs to make, what it sells for, and what it leaves you. The menu matrix sorts dishes into stars, workhorses, puzzles, and dogs, with a suggestion for each.

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:29.844
Profit, like sales, is for System Admins, unless they open sales to everyone. And you can always just tell Assist: we got four cases of oat milk.

